Xalo Xozyana bi çi meşhûr e?
 
Uncle, what is Xozyana famous for?

84
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Wal meşhûr e bi gûza, meşhûr e bi behîva...
 
Well, it is famous for walnuts, famous for almonds...

85
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Meşhûr e bi zeytûna, bi gah e, bi jîn e...
 
Famous for olives, for cattle, for life...

86
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Wal maşalla.
 
Well mashallah.

87
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Tirşê wan maşhûr e.
 
Their pickles are famous.

88
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Simaq meşhûr e ne?
 
Sumac is famous, right?

89
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Simaq meşhûr e.
 
Sumac is famous.

90
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Ez dibêm ba'dîna cema'etê me tim dihatin tirş dikirrin vî
derê.
 
I say, our group from Badina always came to buy pickles
here.

91
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Xalo xê nav lê kirin Xozyana? Tu vî ekê zanî?
 
Uncle, why did they name it Xozyana? Do you know this one?

92
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Welle...
 
Well...

93
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Her halê new le vêderê... Tu kefte bîra te ne?
 
Anyway, in this place... Did you remember it?

94
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Belê, kefte bîra min. Eve xozan e, xozan e dîtin? Xozan.
 
Yes, I remembered. This is a stubble field, did you see the
