Hewşa me derkeve ne?
 
Our courtyard should appear, right?

302
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Wele nise.
 
Well, half of it.

303
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:36,000
E... Çane?
 
Eh... How is it?

304
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:38,000
Maşalla cîkî xweş e.
 
Mashallah, it is a nice place.

305
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:39,000
Ev bêder e jêra dibên.
 
This is a threshing floor, as they call it.

306
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Abo bêder e?
 
Oh, is it a threshing floor?

307
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:42,000
Erê erê, ev no bêder e.
 
Yes, yes, right now this is a threshing floor.

308
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:44,000
Bêder ne... berê vir çi dikirin?
 
Threshing floor... what did they use to do here before?

309
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:48,000
Berê genim, ceh, daxil tînon, şer dikutan.
 
In the past, wheat, barley, crops were brought, they
threshed the city [harvest].

310
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Dikutan, da... carcar e ne?
 
They threshed... with the machine, right?

311
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:50,000
Erê carcar dikutan...
 
Yes, they threshed with the machine...

312
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Ah maşalla, hey bavê min vê tabîetê bigre.
 
Ah Mashallah, hey my father [cameraman], capture this
nature.

313
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:03,000
Maşalla.
 
Mashallah.

314
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:07,000
Leglegê xweş e, mi qe curo nedî vê gundo.
 
The storks are nice, I haven't seen this kind in this
village.

315
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:27,000
Qe ne xêra we ye ji gundo dibînim.
 
Thanks to you, I am seeing the village.

316
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:55,000
Maşalla.
 
Mashallah.

317
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Arê li vî derê jî em li pêşiya mala Apo Rezan ne.
 
Yes, here we are in front of Uncle Rezan's house.

318
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:40,000
Silavê me ji miletê vî gundî re giya re hene, çûçik mezin,
çi dûr dibe çi nêzîk dibe.
 
Our greetings to all the people of this village, small and
big, whether far or near.

319
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Birakî min Rezan, avo emê can xoltîkê ne.
 
My brother Rezan, here we are with the dear Auntie.

320
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Xoltîk, were boy boy ke.
 
Auntie, come show yourself [pose].

321
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Silava were bêjin, ey pîrejinê.
 
Give your greetings, oh old woman.

322
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:53,000
Silavê me ji wa giya ra hene, ji mezin ra, ji wa ra, ey dûr
ra, ey nêzîk ra.
 
Our greetings to all of them, to the big ones, to those, oh
the far ones, oh the near ones.

323
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:56,000
Inşalla hûn werin cî, destê me ba bigrin, eywan afrînê xwe.
 
God willing you come to the place, hold our hands, those
Afrin people of ours.

324
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:58,000
Inşalla, bi izna Xwedê. Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike de.
 
God willing, with God's permission. May God give you a long
life.

325
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Xwedê ji we razî be, sax bin.
 
May God be pleased with you, be healthy.

326
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:01,000
Ew Apo Rezan vo.
 
That was Uncle Rezan.

327
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:03,000
Xwedê ji wa razî be.
 
May God be pleased with them.

328
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Xoltîk, mi tabe'a nîne ez a? Timla mi sêr dike?
 
Auntie, I don't have a follower/fan? Do you watch me?

329
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Wele ney, ez pûş im, heta tu kuderê dikşîne, wele sêr dikim.
 
No by God, I am just sitting, wherever you film, by God I
watch.

330
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:14,000
E ma jî go heme xoro, têkine em Rezan, mlo hew jî vê cûrê,
li xo sêr ke.
 
Well I said, look here, look at Rezan, look at the house in
this way, watch yourself.

331
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:15,000
Ha? Bibîne zikra.
 
Huh? Let it be a memory.

332
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Wî, ez jê hez dikim ji vî tiştî.
 
Oh, I love this thing.

333
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

334
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:19,000
Kîke bimin zikra.
 
Let it remain a memory for me.

335
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:24,000
Qeyses bî me, wek demê va dikir, ez tim sêr dikim heta tu
poşêt tînî.
 
[Unclear] me, like when they did this, I always watch until
you bring the bag/end.

336
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Ha, Xwedê siheta te xweş te de, Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike de.
 
Ha, may God give you good health, may God give you a long
life.

337
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:28,000
Xwedê ji te razî be, dest û lingê te sax bin.
 
May God be pleased with you, may your hands and feet be
healthy.

338
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Tu kurê qîzka min î.
 
You are the son of my daughter.

339
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:34,000
Arê havû li vî derê jî, Apo Rezan bes mar vê îşaretê manasê
ban hewal da, hewalî me war.
 
Yes, friends, here too, Uncle Rezan just gave us the meaning
of this sign, my friend come.

340
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:36,000
Hewşe te kevnor e?
 
Is your courtyard ancient?

341
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,000
Kevnor e.
 
Ancient.

342
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:39,000
Xolo li vî derkê şêr hatine kuştin?
 
Uncle, were lions killed at this spot/door?

343
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:41,000
Vir şêr hatine kuştin.
 
Lions were killed here.

344
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:41,000
Û vir jî şêr hatine?
 
Really?

345
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Û vir jî şêr hatine?
 
And lions came here too?

346
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:43,000
Û vir şêr hatine kuştin.
 
And lions were killed here.

347
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:45,000
Û urte jî çiye nivîsiye?
 
And what is written up there?

348
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:48,000
Nivîsiye Lailahaillallah, Muhemed Resulullah.
 
It is written "There is no god but God, Muhammad is the
Messenger of God."

349
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:50,000
Ewa. Û vir jî suretî têra ye?
 
Really. And here is there a picture/date on it?

350
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Sin tisa' mîye wahid wa sittîn.
 
Year nine hundred and sixty-one [1961 - Arabic].

351
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:54,000
Tisa' mîye wahid wa sittîn.
 
Nine hundred and sixty-one.

352
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:54,000
Emrê xwe çiqso sale wane o?
 
Meaning...

353
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Emrê xwe çiqso sale wane o?
 
How many years old is it?

354
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:58,000
Teqrîben nûd...
 
Approximately ninety...

355
00:33:58,000 --> 00:33:59,000
Nûd?
 
Ninety?

356
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Na.
 
No.

357
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:02,000
Şêst û pênc sal e.
 
Sixty-five years.

358
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:04,000
Şêst û pênc sal e.
 
Sixty-five years.

359
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,000
Û ev îşaretê têr?
 
And these signs on it?

360
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Têr ev jî têr e, têrî sûre çêkirin e.
 
On it, this is also on it, they made it with red
[stone/paint].

361
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:10,000
Wala Apo Rezan hewşek te kevnor e.
 
By God Uncle Rezan, your courtyard is ancient.

362
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:12,000
Birakî min Rezan hewşê xwe sêr ke were.
 
My brother Rezan, come look at your courtyard.

363
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:16,000
Were hewşê Rezan darxe vêro. Mlo bîra gundê xwe kirî, bîra
mala xwe kirî.
 
Come, show Rezan's courtyard here. Look, he misses his
village, he misses his home.

364
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:17,000
Ah...
 
Ah...

365
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:21,000
Maşalla.
 
Mashallah.

366
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:25,000
Çi dortiyê di virdo çêbûye.
 
What a mess/ruin has happened here.

367
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Havûlo, şta ez jî gundo hez dikim, aşiqê gundo dibim.
 
Friends, look, I also love the village, I fall in love with
the village.

368
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Maşalla.
 
Mashallah.

369
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:32,000
Ah, ji birakî min Rezan ra bisewirîn, ha.
 
Ah, let's film for my brother Rezan, here.

370
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Ah.
 
Ah.

371
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:40,000
Rezan heva hewşo wey?
 
Rezan, is this your courtyard?

372
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:42,000
Ha.
 
Ha.

373
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:44,000
Ha.
 
Ha.

374
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Bira jî ew heye.
 
Brother, there is that too.

375
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:48,000
Vêro... navî vî çi dikirin moncî xalo?
 
Here... what did they call this [niche/cupboard] uncle?

376
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,000
Vêra dibên dulab.
 
They call this a "dolab" [cupboard].

377
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,000
Dulab?
 
Cupboard?

378
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:51,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

379
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Hey ovel dikşîne.
 
Hey, it pulls the air/breeze.

380
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:53,000
Ovel dikşîne.
 
It pulls the air.

381
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Hmm.
 
Hmm.

382
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:56,000
Maşalla.
 
Mashallah.

383
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:58,000
Vanda çi cewekî xweş e xweş.
 
Look what a very nice atmosphere.

384
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:01,000
Ehê!
 
Ehey!

385
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:07,000
Havalî min wer jivir va jî hena hewşê gind bigir.
 
My friend, come back here and capture the courtyard of the
village.

386
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,000
Mê qaweta vaxor.
 
We drank coffee.

387
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:11,000
Wele hî saet xweş ne manoko vaxor û bimar o jî heye.
 
By God, good health [thanks] we didn't drink [your] coffee
and there is an excuse too.

388
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:13,000
E min ji se vaxor.
 
Eh, I drank three.

389
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:14,000
Xwedê ji te razî be Apo Rezan, saet xweş.
 
May God be pleased with you Uncle Rezan, good health.

390
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:16,000
Wele min qawet kerem kirine.
 
By God, you offered me coffee.

391
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:17,000
No no xoltîk saet xweş Apo Rezan.
 
No no Auntie, good health Uncle Rezan.

392
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Ne te qawe kîşkiro çi kîşkiro...
 
No, you didn't pull [drink] coffee or pull anything...

393
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,000
Wele...
 
By God...

394
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Yek çûn cem hev, abûjyar qawa nadame.
 
One went to each other, [unclear] didn't give me coffee.

395
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:23,000
No no no, Xwedê ji te razî be, no na.
 
No no no, may God be pleased with you, no no.

396
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Pir kef xweş min bita ro, û Xwedê emrê ki dirêj bita de.
 
I was very happy with you, and may God give you a long life.

397
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:27,000
Ewa çî dikî şele.
 
What are you doing with the basket.

398
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:29,000
Wakî dibê sok min ma vaxor.
 
As if to say, look, I didn't drink.

399
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Nûriya cema'et ba dîna nûrî.
 
Nuri brought the group, Nuri.

400
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:32,000
Nûrî kê?
 
Who is Nuri?

401
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:33,000
Buwajî duxle.
 
The one who enters the duty/shop.

402
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:34,000
Malo?
 
Really?

403
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,000
Dikanê veke.
 
He opens the shop.

404
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:39,000
Buwajî? Malo xolfûrê ber xezanê o vê.
 
The one on duty? Look, the hole/pit in front of that
treasury.

405
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:41,000
Buwajî li Efrînê rûdiniye.
 
The one on duty lives in Afrin.

406
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Efrînê?
 
Afrin?

407
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:45,000
Nûredîn çi ke navî...
 
Nureddin is his name...

408
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:49,000
Xolo, a dibêm gundo, wek noka vî gundî...
 
Uncle, I say the village, like now this village...

409
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Gerek mar û du bizin, mirîşk hebin...
 
Needs to have snakes and two goats, chickens...

410
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:53,000
Dew û rî mer o hebe.
 
One should have yogurt and butter.

411
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:59,000
Vil gundo kes nemaye, şêlke hebe, îşta lê, mewaşî ke hebe.
 
Nobody is left in this village, if there is a kid [goat],
look, if there is livestock.

412
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:01,000
E.
 
Yeah.

413
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Hî kes nene li gundo, kes nemaye.
 
There is nobody in the village, nobody is left.

414
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Maşalla paşko dibe, qicik jî tinene.
 
Mashallah it happens later, there aren't even small
children.

415
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:07,000
Qicik tinene, rast e.
 
There aren't small children, that's true.

416
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:09,000
Yok, kulik mûyî, yo bîstî, yo sîhî...
 
No, all of them, the 20-year-olds, the 30-year-olds...

417
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:12,000
E canik çûn derve o, gî çûn derve.
 
Eh the young people went abroad, they all went abroad.

418
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Dûr welat o ketin e.
 
They fell into distant countries.

419
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:15,000
Ez dibêm şta gerek gih hebe.
 
I say look there should be grass/pasture.

420
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:19,000
No pir gunda dikevime, ez dibêm cahkê benî beşer tina.
 
No, I enter many villages, I say there isn't a single human
being.

421
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:21,000
A çûm Cehko, benî beşer tina ji gundê Cehko.
 
Look I went to Cehko [village name], there isn't a human
being in the village of Cehko.

422
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:22,000
No lo?
 
No man?

423
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Wele ne, yak.
 
By God no, one.

424
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,000
E.
 
Yeah.

425
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:27,000
Gindina jî heye dikavime, yane vê gindî giştik yo di mal
nawetin e bes.
 
There are villages I enter, meaning in this whole village
only two houses stay there.

426
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:31,000
No gundî me... teqrîben gotin, teqrîben...
 
No our village... approximately they said, approximately...

427
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:32,000
Yak yak jê man.
 
One by one they remained.

428
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,000
E.
 
Yeah.

429
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:37,000
Zortir henek jihanin ji berê da, zortir yo li Helebê
rûniştin e, yo jolo çûne Ewropa.
 
Many of them are from before, many were living in Aleppo, or
they went to Europe from there.

430
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,000
Erê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

431
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:39,000
Maşalla, maşalla.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

432
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:42,000
Wele rup germik e sokme ovîna maşalla.
 
By God, a warm sun is on us like love, Mashallah.

433
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Dû dêmkê ser me ra beqetînin, em çûn çeqmoqo.
 
Let two moments pass over us, we went to the lighter
[location/item].

434
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Dînê dîman sor.
 
Look, the view is red.

435
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:50,000
Vir sor e jiko.
 
Here is red too.

436
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:53,000
Xolo hunê avê... ewa hunê baranê bardinê?
 
Uncle, you... the water... do you drink/collect the rain
water?

437
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Hanefî ye?
 
Is it tap water?

438
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Xolo vê baran em bardinê, hanefî jê.
 
Uncle, we drink this rain [water], tap water too.

439
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:57,000
Hanefî heye?
 
Is there tap water?

440
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:58,000
E rinda.
 
Yeah, it's good.

441
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Tasek av bide me xoltîk, tasek av.
 
Give us a cup of water Auntie, a cup of water.

442
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:05,000
Ah.
 
Ah.

443
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:07,000
Arê wele.
 
Yes by God.

444
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:09,000
Rûk xweş e gundo, gundo şta, wuno...
 
The face of the village is nice, the village look, like
this...

445
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:14,000
Ta korî xo xolos kir, qortox kor no me, çkê xororûnê şta.
 
You finished your blind [work], blind work is not for us,
because sit down look.

446
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:15,000
Kê... kê veçe ne wey xol?
 
Who... whose grandchildren are these uncle?

447
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Lê?
 
Huh?

448
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:18,000
E.
 
Yeah.

449
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:20,000
Tab'an xoltîk jî xok e... na xok e xut?
 
Of course Auntie is also earth [native/humble]... isn't she
earth herself?

450
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:21,000
Erê erê.
 
Yes, yes.

451
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:23,000
Mago belkîm deko rezen e.
 
I said maybe she is the mother of the vineyards.

452
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:24,000
O...
 
Oh...

453
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Li xokomine e.
 
She is of my earth/land.

454
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:28,000
Xwedê emrê ki dirêj pê de.
 
May God give her a long life.

455
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:31,000
Xoltîk boy boy ke, qîs ke, boy boy ke.
 
Auntie show yourself, speak, show yourself.

456
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:33,000
Arê.
 
Yes.

457
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Xwedê sihetek xweş bo we de, Xwedê emrê ki dirêj bo we de.
 
May God give you good health, may God give you a long life.

458
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:39,000
E.
 
Yeah.

459
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:44,000
E we xolê wey çoye, hûn rindin e, rihetin e, îşê we çon e?
 
Eh, how is your situation, are you good, are you
comfortable, how is your work?

460
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Silavê me ji wa giya ra hene.
 
Our greetings to all of them.

461
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Ji dûr waro toro, ji xerîb waro toro.
 
To those coming from afar, to those coming from
exile/foreign lands.

462
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:52,000
Ji b... tirkiya... bajaroro.
 
From... Turkey... to the cities.

463
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:55,000
Hûn gulea gulea inşalla werin Efrîna xwe.
 
May you, flower by flower, God willing come to your Afrin.

464
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Xwedê destê me ba bigîne.
 
May God let us hold hands.

465
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Ya rebî alemnî, Xwedê rê ke rind pîşê me ke inşalla.
 
Amen.

466
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:01,000
Ya rebî alemnî, Xwedê rê ke rind pîşê me ke inşalla.
 
Oh Lord of the worlds, may God place a good path before us
God willing.

467
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:02,000
Serketin be.
 
May there be success.

468
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:03,000
Hmm.
 
Hmm.

469
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:05,000
Inşalla Xwedê siheta te xweş bide.
 
God willing may God give you good health.

470
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:07,000
Destî dûr û nêzîko ba bigîne.
 
May He let the hands of the far and near hold each other.

471
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:09,000
Em jwa rozî ne, Xwedê jwa rozî be.
 
We are pleased with you, may God be pleased with you.

472
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:09,000
Hûn qewata me ne, hûn dota me ne, hûn tate... ma inşalla
tênder.
 
Amen.

473
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:12,000
Hûn qewata me ne, hûn dota me ne, hûn tate... ma inşalla
tênder.
 
You are our strength, you are our daughters, you are... well
God willing inside.

474
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:16,000
Em veeqetîn û hûn barî me ra dikin, saeta we gya xweş be.
 
We were separated and you are carrying our burden, may your
health be very good.

475
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:20,000
Em jê razî ne. Saeta we gya xweş, cabiya gya moş dikim ne.
 
We are pleased with it. May your health be very good, I kiss
all your foreheads right.

476
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:23,000
Xoltîk, e... em guftinke şta vrs kin.
 
Auntie, uh... let's cut a conversation/chat now.

477
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Xoltîk bereke, emr çand e ne, eta?
 
Auntie blessed one, how much is the age/how old are you,
you?

478
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:29,000
Wele hene belkî şêst, şa şêst, heftê me.
 
Well there are maybe sixty, sixty-six, I am seventy.

479
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Heftê?
 
Seventy?

480
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:31,000
Heftê pênc.
 
Seventy-five.

481
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:35,000
Xoltîk, e... berê xweş bû lê noka xweş e?
 
Auntie, uh... was the past good or is now good?

482
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:39,000
Wele berê jî ne ko xweş tî bû, bes cefo pir bû.
 
Well, the past wasn't that 'goodness', but the
suffering/hardship was a lot.

483
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:41,000
Berê xweş bû, beş cefo pir bû.
 
The past was good, but the hardship was a lot.

484
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:42,000
Tuno yanî cefo pir bû.
 
Not there, meaning hardship was a lot.

485
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:44,000
Îşta diçûn peliye.
 
Look, they went for husks/gathering.

486
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:47,000
Takra deştê tînon, şev ra bar dikirin.
 
Brought loads from the plain, carried loads at night.

487
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:49,000
Dibirin ser bêderê, dikutan.
 
Took to the threshing floor, threshed.

488
00:38:49,000 --> 00:38:54,000
Li ba dikirin, genim donîn dişuştin, bulxur dikelandin.
 
Winnowed [separated grain from chaff], put down wheat and
washed it, boiled bulgur.

489
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:58,000
Dibirin êş, manan dikir bi sêlê, bi têxt.
 
Took to the mill, made bread on the griddle, on the sheet.

490
00:38:58,000 --> 00:39:00,000
Me dibrûştî no dikir.
 
We made roasted [food].

491
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:04,000
Îşta me kitaw dikirin, me yexnê fosûlo dikirin.
 
Look we made dumplings/meatballs, we made bean stew.

492
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:05,000
Gerîma roş dikirin.
 
We made sun-dried food.

493
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:07,000
Hûn tim rehet bûn ne?
 
You were always comfortable right?

494
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:07,000
Kareba tunebû.
 
What?

495
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:09,000
Kareba tunebû.
 
There was no electricity.

496
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:10,000
Alet malat jî tunebû ne?
 
There were no appliances/machines either right?

497
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:13,000
Kareba tunebû, wextê kî şûnda kareba hat.
 
There was no electricity, when electricity came later.

498
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:16,000
Kareba selaftine bî, xweşiya kareba hat wele rind bû.
 
Electricity was [unclear word], the goodness of electricity
came, well it was good.

499
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:20,000
Noka jî dinya rind bûye, tam nemaye, heyat nemaye.
 
Now the world has become good, [but] no taste remains, no
life remains.

500
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:21,000
Emr nemaye.
 
No age/lifespan remains.

501
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:23,000
Dinya rind bûye, halê me jî nemaye.
 
The world became good, but we have no strength/state left.

502
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:26,000
Maşalla, te dîn wakî çi çako ye, Xwedê emrê ki dirêj bita
de.
 
Mashallah, you look like a very good person, may God give
you a long life.

503
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:28,000
Dil namre, xoltîk, dil namre.
 
The heart doesn't die, Auntie, the heart doesn't die.

504
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:29,000
E.
 
Yeah.

505
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:32,000
Hemdilla îşta barê ona bî, raje bîn.
 
Thank God look the load was like that, we were content.

506
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:34,000
Di mist kalone... diçûn tirê diçinîn.
 
In the fist of the old men... we went and picked grapes.

507
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:40,000
E xoltîk noka, e noka gitişt hozir in, mite wafire, û hîn na
rozî nî jî.
 
Eh Auntie now, eh now everything is ready, available, and
still you aren't satisfied.

508
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:43,000
Lê, raje bîn, diçûn qoper dikirin.
 
What, we were content, we went and piled/gathered.

509
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Şev hiltînon, dikalsandin.
 
Picked up at night, piled up.

510
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:52,000
O takra, îşta e... mêwe, doxe, bowerê, çil û biçiniyona.
 
And up to, look uh... fruit, buttermilk, believe me, forty
[unclear] picked them.

511
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:56,000
Razê biçiniyona, bi tirikirona, bi mûş kirona.
 
Picked the vineyard, made into grapes, made into [unclear].

512
00:39:56,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Arde vadona ox, û safî çêkron, zeyt û...
 
Gave the flour/ground [unclear], and made clear, oil and...

513
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:03,000
Û sûda dikirin û wî alî va.
 
And they made use of it over that side.

514
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:07,000
Paşê xata didan, dikirin serê oxê, paşê me dikir loqê.
 
Then they laid out the lines, put it at the edge of the
furrow, and then we made it into bundles.

515
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:10,000
Paşê tirî diçnîn, dikirin dims.
 
Then they picked grapes and made molasses.

516
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:14,000
Dimsê xwe dikelandin, ê wexta dikirin şîşê, difrotin.
 
They boiled their molasses, then put it in bottles and sold
it.

517
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:16,000
Ê hefsidê dikirin, pêt...
 
They made sour pomegranate sauce, pulp...

518
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:18,000
Hesab diçûyî zeytûna...
 
The account [work] went to the olives...

519
00:40:18,000 --> 00:40:20,000
Ê, hesabê zeytûna jî hebûn, cîran dihatin cem hev.
 
Yes, there was the olive work too, neighbors would come
together.

520
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:24,000
Em diçûn ka, mesqere, şûxul dikirin.
 
We went to the threshing floor, joking around, doing the
work.

521
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Sihet jî hebû, ne?
 
There was health back then too, right?

522
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:29,000
Lêê, na wekî noko bûn... noko kûk, kûk, kûk...
 
Oh, no, they weren't like now... now it is [cough, cough,
cough]...

523
00:40:29,000 --> 00:40:32,000
Na tamê dinê mayî, na xêr bereket mayî.
 
Neither the taste of the world remains, nor the blessing
remains.

524
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:33,000
Na tu tiştek nema ye.
 
Nothing remains.

525
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:37,000
Waa, em bêjin xweşbîn e... Xwedê tiştê qenc bike.
 
Wow, let's say we are optimistic... May God make things
good.

526
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:41,000
Xwedê sihetê xweş bide, Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike.
 
May God give good health, may God give you a long life.

527
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:44,000
Slavên me jî ji gundiyan ra hene, ji cîran û dostan ra hene.
 
We have greetings for the villagers, for the neighbors and
friends.

528
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:48,000
Çiqas cîran û dost û nas û welatan e, ji gişta re hene.
 
However many neighbors, friends, acquaintances, and
compatriots there are, greetings to all of them.

529
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:51,000
Emrê Xwedê li bavê te be, hewa jî birakê min e.
 
May God have mercy on your father, and he is my brother too.

530
00:40:51,000 --> 00:40:54,000
Ez jî heme, pênc qîçikê min jî hene.
 
I am here too, and I have five children.

531
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:56,000
Xwedê giyan şîfa bide, çavê qîçikê te giyan maç dikim.
 
May God give healing to their souls, I kiss the eyes of all
your children.

532
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:59,000
Çavê te jî maç dikim, Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike.
 
I kiss your eyes too, may God prolong your life.

533
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:03,000
Erê Abol no, berê cefaf pirr bî.
 
Yes Uncle Abol, in the past there was a lot of hardship.

534
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Ê noko maşallah, her tişt mutevefir e.
 
But now, mashallah, everything is available.

535
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:10,000
Em bi telefon ne, em bi kereba ne, bi înternet ne.
 
We are on telephones, we are with electricity, with
internet.

536
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:11,000
Em bi her hesabî ne.
 
We are on every account.

537
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:13,000
Û hîna em, ew jî noka, elhemdulillah, elhemdulillah ji Xwedê
re.
 
And still we, even now, praise be to God, praise be to God.

538
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:15,000
Hemd ji Xwedê re.
 
Praise be to God.

539
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Na noko, xwarin noko em noka ne...
 
No, now, the food now, we are just [eating] now...

540
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:23,000
Fa xwarin, fa xwarin... çûndin na ye, tişte wekî berê.
 
Just eating, just eating... there is no going [working],
things aren't like before.

541
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:27,000
Yên ew anha cîran pirr bûn, recam cîran...
 
Those neighbors back then were many, visiting neighbors...

542
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:31,000
Dûra şabûna hez nakan, wekî berê êvarê li hev rûniştin.
 
Now they don't like joy, like before when they sat together
in the evening.

543
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:32,000
Tiştê berê nemaye.
 
The things of the past remain no more.

544
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:34,000
Qeswet pirr bûn xaltîkê, qeswet pirr bûn.
 
The worries were many auntie, the worries were many.

545
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Berê qeswet, mesele wena zîde tune bî.
 
Before, worries, for example, things weren't this excessive.

546
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:40,000
Xel... însan mirtah bî, diçûn cem hevdu dadin.
 
Peop... humans were at ease, they went to sit with each
other.

547
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:46,000
Ê noko her kes dibêje 'Allahumma nefsî', her yek serê xwe
dinê ser balgê xwe bi derdê xwe da keti noko.
 
But now everyone says 'Oh God, myself' [selfishness],
everyone puts their head on their pillow falling into their
own troubles now.

548
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:48,000
Tiştekî darbaz be, dîsa elhemdulillah.
 
It's something that passes, still praise be to God.

549
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:51,000
Bêguman dîsa elhemdulillah, elhemdulillah, elhemdulillah.
 
Undoubtedly, still praise be to God, praise be to God,
praise be to God.

550
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:53,000
Dîsa em silavan li gundê xwe ne, li malê xwe ne.
 
Again, we send greetings to our village, to our homes.

551
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:56,000
Em silavan li Efrîna xwe ne, em sibe da Efrîna xwe jî êvarê
tên.
 
We send greetings to our Afrin, we come to our Afrin in the
morning and evening.

552
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:58,000
Saet xweş, Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike.
 
Good health, may God prolong your life.

553
00:41:58,000 --> 00:42:18,000
Saet xweş, Xwedê ji te razî be. Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike,
Xwedê we mihafeze ke.
 
Good health, may God be pleased with you. May God prolong
your life, may God protect you.

554
00:49:40,000 --> 00:49:45,000
Erê Abol no! Li vê derê jî birayê min...
 
Yes Uncle Abol! Here too my brother...

555
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:48,000
...cot dajot, joti dêwir.
 
...was plowing, plowing the fallow land.

556
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:50,000
Te dît dewrî qabaye?
 
Did you see the turning around?

557
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:52,000
Îgê hende, ew ne hewşo kar nê.
 
Look right here, that is not exactly [good] work.

558
00:49:52,000 --> 00:49:55,000
Eke şûna cîckê xetkê bojim...
 
If I draw a line where the planter/chickpea was...

559
00:49:55,000 --> 00:49:57,000
Qolayî lê çetin in.
 
It looks easy but it is difficult.

560
00:49:57,000 --> 00:50:00,000
Berî vê min ceriband, tim hizkî min dibiya...
 
Before this I tried it, I always liked it...

561
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:04,000
Qulibî be, erd jê qul î ye. De... Çû.
 
It might tip over, the ground is steep. Come on... It went.

562
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:08,000
Yalla. Maşallah. Bide sekinandin.
 
Come on. Mashallah. Stop it.

563
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:10,000
Jêr na, yê jêr.
 
Not down, the lower one.

564
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:13,000
Ha?
 
Huh?

565
00:50:13,000 --> 00:50:15,000
Yo... Ji xetê derket.
 
Oh... It went out of the line.

566
00:50:15,000 --> 00:50:18,000
Rak, xet rast. Çû... De...
 
Stop, straight line. It went... Come on...

567
00:50:18,000 --> 00:50:21,000
Ewa, tikan bide wekî direksûn. Ewaaa.
 
Yes, turn it a bit like a steering wheel. Yesss.

568
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:25,000
O bo... Xayê divê pa... uşşş.
 
Oh man... The guy needs to... shhh.

569
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:28,000
Divê karek na, korê te ye?
 
He doesn't need a job, is he your blind one?

570
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:29,000
Korê te ye?
 
Is he your blind one?

571
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:30,000
(Unintelligible)
 
(Unintelligible)

572
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:32,000
Derdikeve.
 
It's coming out.

573
00:50:32,000 --> 00:50:34,000
Wera...
 
Come...

574
00:50:34,000 --> 00:50:37,000
Ewa alem î, ez zanim. Maşallah.
 
Yes he is blind, I know. Mashallah.

575
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:43,000
Welle ez e... e... ebi çil hî... hekî yek sal e dajo.
 
Well I... uh... uh... for forty... about one year I've been
driving.

576
00:50:43,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Çil û yek sal ne? Bereka emr çend e?
 
41 years right? How much is the blessing of age (how old are
you)?

577
00:50:46,000 --> 00:50:49,000
Lê... o... o... çil hî... yek helo ko...
 
But... oh... oh... forty... one...

578
00:50:49,000 --> 00:50:52,000
Xwedê ji te razî be. Sed xwe, sedê te xweş. Serkeftin be ji
te re.
 
May God be pleased with you. A hundred yourself, your
hundred is good. Success to you.

579
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:55,000
Zor şad a yabo. De şad a yabo... Xera.
 
Very happy oh father. So happy oh father... Good.

580
00:50:55,000 --> 00:51:01,000
Here.
 
Go.

581
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,000
Li jêr botim.
 
I put it in low gear.

582
00:51:02,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Ewa, here, here, here, here.
 
Yes, go, go, go, go.

583
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:10,000
Hey... Welle çetin e. Alo se'dê wana be.
 
Hey... By God it's difficult. May God help them.

584
00:51:10,000 --> 00:51:15,000
O bo... Çû. Kufte, filtî, filtî, filtî.
 
Oh man... It went. It stalled, slipped, slipped, slipped.

585
00:51:15,000 --> 00:51:17,000
Uşşş. Uşşş. Uşşş.
 
Shhh. Shhh. Shhh.

586
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:21,000
Xayo ez nizanim, ya xayo. Rak.
 
Brother I don't know, oh brother. Stop.

587
00:51:21,000 --> 00:51:24,000
Havna alem î ne, korê xan e? Ez nizanim.
 
Is this guy not blind, blind from home? I don't know.

588
00:51:24,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Têkê bîn, tim yêmîn... yasor bikşîne.
 
Bring the strap, always right... pull left.

589
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:29,000
Lê... Wekî direksûnî makîneyê. Lê?
 
But... Like the steering of a machine. But?

590
00:51:29,000 --> 00:51:31,000
O ha bo... xwedê zana ye.
 
Oh like that... God is knowledgeable.

591
00:51:31,000 --> 00:51:33,000
Yek sêyê alem î ye?
 
Is he one-third blind?

592
00:51:33,000 --> 00:51:34,000
Lê... we...
 
But... well...

593
00:51:34,000 --> 00:51:37,000
Maşallah. Cotê diewêr jî pir rind e ha bolo.
 
Mashallah. The tractor is also very good oh man.

594
00:51:37,000 --> 00:51:40,000
Xeta bernade, dibar doran ra lê dikave.
 
It doesn't leave the line, it hits the turns well.

595
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:42,000
Çawîre nê lê. Çawîre nê lê.
 
His eyes are not on it. His eyes are not on it.

596
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:46,000
Maşallah, maşallah. Xwedê quwetê bide, bide.
 
Mashallah, mashallah. May God give strength, give.

597
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:48,000
Lê... owî... rak...
 
But... he... lift...

598
00:51:48,000 --> 00:52:08,000
Rak... kişşş...
 
Lift... pull...

599
00:52:10,000 --> 00:52:30,000
(Music)
 
(Music)

600
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:56,000
Erê hevalno, li vê derkê jî, em li biniya Xoziyana ne.
 
Yes friends, at this spot too, we are below Xoziyana.

601
00:52:56,000 --> 00:53:00,000
Virmek bazik heye, kavnor e. Darik heye, bîrê avê heye.
 
There is a tomb here, it's old. There is a tree, there is a
water well.

602
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:03,000
Em li vî derkî gihîştin dawiya vîdyoya xwe.
 
We reached the end of our video at this spot.

603
00:53:03,000 --> 00:53:08,000
Tab'en li vê derkê malik ji me xwestibûn. Malê Ehmed Bozo.
 
Of course, at this spot a family had asked for us. The
family of Ahmed Bozo.

604
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:13,000
E me disê meriyo pirskir, hinekî go rehmetî bî, hinekî go
hewşê xwo jor e...
 
We asked the man again, some said he was deceased, some said
his yard is up...

605
00:53:13,000 --> 00:53:16,000
E maro, me nekarî tê derxista.
 
Oh man, we couldn't figure it out.

606
00:53:16,000 --> 00:53:20,000
Da şola hewşa gundê derketibe. Ez zanim, ma te hewş bar
nedan?
 
Since the issue of the village yard came out. I know, didn't
you move the yard?

607
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:22,000
Milo qisûrî me ci efû kin.
 
Forgive our shortcomings.

608
00:53:22,000 --> 00:53:27,000
Kesê ji me xwestî, malê Ehmed Bozo, çavê gindê maçî dikim.
 
The person who asked us, family of Ahmed Bozo, I kiss the
eyes of the village.

609
00:53:27,000 --> 00:53:31,000
Qisûrî efû ke. Şarê xwe jî pir teng bûn.
 
Forgive the fault. Their streets were very narrow.

610
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:34,000
Teng bûn şarê gundê. Tuzanî şarê reîsî bes yek bî.
 
The village streets were narrow. You know the main street
was only one.

611
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:37,000
Û hisê... ewê mijî tê, duzonî?
 
And the sound... that thing comes, you know?

612
00:53:37,000 --> 00:53:42,000
Milefrîn çêkir, e dû milefrîn çêkir, e dîsa hisê xirxirta jê
tê.
 
Fixed the muffler, fixed the muffler again, and still the
rattling sound comes from it.

613
00:53:42,000 --> 00:53:44,000
Tê bê ne zaptî ye.
 
Come see it's not fixed.

614
00:53:44,000 --> 00:53:48,000
Wole ev fîltî çiye? O bo...
 
By God what is this escaped part? Oh man...

